        "original_id": "b51358c8-430e-53b0-a9ef-8ea99e2af829",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ogallala, Keith County, Nebraska, Great Plains, East Omaha\n- Systems: Ogallala Aquifer\n- Organizations: Sherman Elementary School\n- Topics: Texas High Plains AVA, vineyard irrigation\n\nFacts:\n- Ogallala is a city in Keith County, Nebraska, United States.\n- The Ogallala Aquifer is a shallow water table aquifer beneath the Great Plains in the United States, surrounded by sand, silt, clay, and gravel.\n- In the Texas High Plains AVA, most vineyards are irrigated with water from the Ogallala Aquifer because the plains can be extremely dry.\n- Sherman Elementary School is located at 5618 North 14th Avenue in East Omaha, Nebraska, United States.",
